== Stamps == <!--T:57-->
</translate>
<noinclude>{{Comseealso|Commons:Stamps/Public domain}}</noinclude>

[[File:Red copyright.svg|25px|link=|Copyrighted]] <translate><!--T:58-->
According to the TIPO<tvar name="ref"><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tipo.gov.tw/tw/copyright/692-11911.html|title=電子郵件920523|work=TIPO|date=2003-05-23}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tipo.gov.tw/tw/copyright/692-15590.html|title=電子郵件1061212|work=TIPO|date=2017-12-12}}</ref></tvar>, stamps are generally considered copyrighted artworks in Taiwan if their designs possess '''originality''' and '''creativity''' and are not classified as '''official documents''' under Article 9, Paragraph 1, Item 1 of the Copyright Act. Stamps classified as official documents, such as those issued by government agencies that serve as official notices or documents, are not subject to copyright protection. However, most stamps, featuring artistic designs, are unlikely to fall under this category and are thus protected by copyright. Old stamps may enter the public domain when their copyright expires, as per the [[#Terms]] section above.

